# EnvHaven Environment

## Quick Reference

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **OS** | Ubuntu (Docker container) |
| **User** | `abc` (sudo available) |
| **Shell** | zsh (oh-my-zsh) or bash |
| **Workspace** | `${WORKSPACE_PATH}` |

### What persists

Your home is `/config`, the only directory mounted from outside the container. **`/config` survives workspace updates and restarts; everything else resets to the image on update.**

| Survives an update? | What |
|---------------------|------|
| **Yes** | Everything under `/config`: your `${WORKSPACE_PATH}` projects, dotfiles, `~/.zshrc`, SSH keys, and `/config/.local/bin` (first on `PATH`) |
| **No** | `apt` packages and anything under `/usr`, `/opt`, `/mise`; global installs (`npm i -g`, `cargo install`, `uv tool install`, `mise use -g`) |

Keep dependencies inside the project: `node_modules`, `.venv`, and Go modules live under `${WORKSPACE_PATH}`, so they persist for free. If you install a global CLI the user will want tomorrow, drop the binary in `/config/.local/bin`. Pre-installed tools always come back; they ship in the image.

### Web Servers

**MUST bind to `0.0.0.0`**, not localhost or 127.0.0.1, for apps to be accessible outside the container. **Default to port 3000** unless the user asks otherwise. When a server is up, hand the user its URL to open, don't just report the port; the exact host is in the Managed or Self-Hosted section at the end of this file (Managed workspaces get an automatic HTTPS preview URL wired to 3000).

```javascript
// Express
app.listen(3000, '0.0.0.0');

// Next.js (package.json)
"scripts": { "dev": "next dev -H 0.0.0.0" }

// Vite (vite.config.ts)
server: { host: '0.0.0.0' }

// FastAPI
uvicorn main:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 3000
```

### Package Managers

| Language | Preferred | Command |
|----------|-----------|---------|
| JavaScript | `bun` | `bun install`, `bun add <pkg>` |
| Python | `uv` | `uv pip install`, `uv add <pkg>` |

### Database

Use **SQLite** by default: `sqlite3 myapp.db`

